Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emajuddin_Ahamed$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Emajuddin%20ahamed.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Writer, Academic$b$, $b$Malda district$b$, NULL, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Faizul Islam$b$, DATE '1963-01-01', DATE '2025-01-21', $b$Faizul Islam (24 November 1963 – 21 January 2025) was a Bangladeshi economist and fiction writer.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faizul_Islam_(writer)$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Short story writer$b$, NULL, NULL, 'year', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Fakhrul Islam Khan$b$, DATE '1925-02-09', DATE '2007-05-13', $b$Fakhrul Islam Khan (known as FI Khan; 9 February 1925 – 13 May 2007) was a Bangladeshi editor, journalist, cultural organizer, playwright, producer, and director. He was the editor of Gulistan (1950), a monthly Bengali magazine, and Kadem (1966), a weekly magazine. He was the joint news editor with Shah Azizur Rahman of the monthly magazine Inqilab (published from Kolkata).  Khan has made a special contribution to Barisal's cultural activities, cultural heritage, literary councils, journalism and Barisal Press Club. He was the first Bengal Muslim film producer. He established Barisal Natya Niketan in 1964.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fakhrul_Islam_Khan$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Journalist, Film producer, Film director, Socio-cultural animator$b$, $b$Barishal$b$, NULL, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Fakhruzzaman Chowdhury$b$, NULL, DATE '2014-06-12', $b$Fakhruzzaman Chowdhury (5 January 1940 – 12 June 2014) was a Bangladeshi author. He served as the director of Bangladesh Television. He was awarded Bangla Academy Literary Award, the highest literary award in Bangladesh in 2005.

Awards: Bangla Academy Literary Award
Education: University of Dhaka

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fakhruzzaman_Chowdhury$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Writer$b$, NULL, NULL, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Farida Majid$b$, DATE '1942-07-27', DATE '2021-09-28', $b$Farida Majid (27 July 1942 – 28 September 2021) was a Bangladeshi poet, translator, and academic.

Part of the first generation of Bangladeshi writers producing English-language work, Majid was an influential member of the London literary scene in the 1970s, when she ran the independent Salamander press. She then spent two decades as a professor of language and culture in New York before returning to Bangladesh in her later years.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farida_Majid$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Writer, Translator, Academic, Poet$b$, $b$Kolkata$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Faruk Quazi$b$, DATE '1949-01-17', DATE '2020-07-03', $b$Faruk Quazi (Bengali: ফারুক কাজী; January 17, 1949 - July 3, 2020) was a Bangladeshi journalist and law reporter. He served Bangladesh Prime Minister as Deputy Press Secretary and Bangladesh High Commission in New Delhi as Press Minister. He was also one of the founders and President of the Law Reporters' Forum of Bangladesh. He was a pioneer law reporter and introduced law reporting by journalists in Bangladesh. He covered the Supreme Court's proceedings since 1972. He covered parliament also.

After returning from Bangladesh Liberation War, 1971, Faruk Quazi joined now-defunct Daily Banglar Bani in 1972. In 1997 he joined Bangladesh Sangbad Songstha and then he was appointed as Deputy Press Secretary of Prime Minister and later on he joined Bangladesh High Commission in New Delhi as Press Minister.  Returning from New Delhi he joined UNB as Chief Correspondents of News and he established with his fellow friends Law Reporters' Forum and became the first President of the forum.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faruk_Quazi$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bangladeshi%20Legal%20Journalist%20Faruk%20Quazi.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Writer$b$, $b$Thanapara$b$, $b$New Elephant road$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Faruq Ahmed Choudhury$b$, DATE '1934-01-04', DATE '2017-05-17', $b$Faruq Ahmed Choudhury (4 January 1934 – 17 May 2017) was a Bangladeshi diplomat. He served as Bangladesh's first Chief of Protocol beginning in 1972, Foreign Secretary from 1984 to 1986, and High Commissioner to India from 1986 to 1992.

Awards: Bangla Academy Literary Award
Education: Sylhet Govt. Pilot High School

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faruq_Ahmed_Choudhury$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Diplomat, Writer$b$, $b$Sribhumi$b$, $b$Dhaka$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Fateh Ali Waisi$b$, DATE '1820-01-01', DATE '1886-01-01', $b$Sayyid Fateh Ali Waisi (1820-1886) was a Sufi saint, preacher of Islam and a Persian-language poet. His epic poem Diwan-i-Waisi, written in Persian, gained widespread popularity. Due to its literary importance, the poem is included in the curricula of various universities, including Dhaka University.

