Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarat_Chandra_Das$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sarat%20Chandra%20Das%2C%20C.I.E.%20photo%20from%20Journey%20to%20Lhasa%20and%20Central%20Tibet%20%28page%2010%20crop%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Explorer, Photographer, Writer, School teacher, Linguist, Spy$b$, $b$Chittagong$b$, $b$Chittagong$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Sarat Chandra Roy$b$, DATE '1871-11-04', DATE '1942-04-30', $b$Sarat Chandra Roy (4 November 1871 – 30 April 1942) was an Indian scholar of anthropology. He is sometimes regarded as the 'father of Indian ethnography', the 'first Indian ethnographer', and as the 'first Indian anthropologist'.

Education: University of Calcutta, Surendranath College, Scottish Church College

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarat_Chandra_Roy$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sarat%20Chandra%20Roy.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Anthropologist, Ethnographer, Writer, Ethnologist$b$, $b$Khulna District$b$, $b$Ranchi$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Sarat Kumar Ray$b$, DATE '1876-01-01', DATE '1946-04-12', $b$Sarat Kumar Ray (Bengali: শরৎ কুমার রায়) (1876–1946) was a member of the royal family of Dighapatia. A noted scholar, he was the son of the Raja (King) Pramathanath Ray and lived in the Maharaja's Palace. Along with historian Ramaprasad Chanda, he co-founded the Varendra Research Museum, which Lord Dundas the Governor of Bengal, inaugurated in November 1919. He was well traveled, and visited England in 1900. He was a friend of Rabindranath Tagore.

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarat_Kumar_Ray$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sarat%20Kumar%20Roy%20%281876-1946%29.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Writer$b$, NULL, NULL, 'year', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Saroj Dutta$b$, DATE '1914-03-13', DATE '1971-08-05', $b$Saroj Dutta (March 13, 1914 – August 5, 1971) popularly known comrade SD, was an Indian communist intellectual and poet, active in the Naxalite movement in West Bengal in the 1960s. He was the first West Bengal state secretary of Communist Party of India (Marxist-Leninist) (CPI(ML)). He also remained editor-in-chief of the Amrita Bazar Patrika during the 1940s.

It is commonly thought that he was killed in a police encounter on August 5, 1971, but till now he was missing in police and state records.

Education: University of Calcutta, Scottish Church College

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saroj_Dutta$b$, 'en', $b$https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Monuments%2C%20statues%20of%20Kolkata%20metropolis%2016.jpg?width=640$b$, $b$Journalist, Translator, Editor, Politician$b$, $b$Jashore District$b$, $b$Kolkata$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Satyananda Giri$b$, DATE '1896-11-17', DATE '1971-08-02', $b$Satyananda Giri (; 17 November 1896 – 2 August 1971) is the monastic name of Manamohan Mazumder, an Indian monk and a monastic disciple of Kriya Yoga guru Swami Sri Yukteswar Giri. He was a close childhood friend of, and brother-disciple to, Paramahansa Yogananda. In his later monastic life, he served as the leader of several yoga training institutions in East India.

Education: University of Calcutta

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satyananda_Giri$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Writer$b$, $b$Bangladesh$b$, $b$Medinipur$b$, 'day', 'day');
INSERT INTO people (id, name, birth_date, death_date, bio, lang, photo_url, occupation, birth_place, death_place, birth_precision, death_precision) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $b$Satyen Sen$b$, DATE '1907-03-28', DATE '1981-01-05', $b$Satyen Sen (Bengali: সত্যেন সেন; 28 March 1907 - 5 January 1981)  was a Bengali revolutionary, writer, and cultural activist who played a vital role in the Indian independence movement and later in post-independence progressive movements. A member of Jugantar revolutionary organisation and later the Communist movement, he spent years in prison and embraced Marxism–Leninism. Sen was a founder of the cultural organisation Bangladesh Udichi Shilpigoshthi and a key figure in the Progressive Writers' Movement. He contributed significantly to literature, workers' mobilisation, and the Bangladesh Liberation War. His work reflected a lifelong commitment to justice, equality, and the upliftment of ordinary people through culture and activism.

Awards: Ekushey Padak, Bangla Academy Literary Award
Education: University of Calcutta

Source: Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satyen_Sen$b$, 'en', NULL, $b$Writer$b$, $b$Munshiganj District$b$, $b$Santiniketan$b$, 'day', 'day');
